First, the Literal Listener (L0) question. A literal listener takes the words at face value. The speaker says "That was easy," so the literal interpretation would be that the action (lifting the cat) was easy. So looking at the options, option d says "The cat was easy to lift up." That seems straightforward. The other options don't directly relate to the action's difficulty. So L0 would pick d.

Next, the Informative Speaker (S1) question.

